    <!-- ROUTING MODE: <trip from=".." to=".."/>, not a fixed <route edges="..">.
     SUMO computes the path at load time, so this survives network edits
     instead of silently breaking like the old hand-typed 4-edge sequence
     (E1, 245250305#20, 245250305#35, 693648180), which was never a
     connected path in the graph.

     E1 direction: the network file has E1 as from="-2948" to="-1531"
     (into the corridor). An earlier comment here claimed E1 had been
     flipped to J2 -> -2948; that is NOT what the network contains. The
     network file is authoritative. Corrected 2026-08-16.

     RETOUR DESTINATION: was to="E9". E9 is unreachable from 693648180
     (verified by BFS and by SUMO itself: "No connection between edge
     693648180 and edge E9 found" -> "has no valid route" -> hard abort).
     E9 is a one-way entry ramp, so it cannot be a destination.
     Provisionally set to E5, the roundabout exit stub, whose end lies
     ~48 m from E1's origin junction -2948 and which IS reachable from
     the corridor. THIS IS A PLACEHOLDER, not a surveyed terminus -
     replace it with the real Bus 25 western terminus.

     Note: XML comments must not contain two consecutive hyphens. The
     previous version of this comment did, which made SUMO abort at load
     time with an "illegal sequence in comment" parse error. -->

